they match the service\'s selector. If the pod\'s labels don\'t match, the service won\'t have endpoints. \n\nSo I need to describe the pod otel-collector-agent-7fmss to check its labels and see if they match the service\'s selector. If they don\'t, that\'s the problem. Also, maybe the deployment for otel-collector isn\'t correctly set up. Alternatively, the pod might be in a CrashLoopBackOff state. Let me check the pod\'s status. \n\nWait, the user previously ran kubectl get pods and saw otel-collector-agent-7fmss as Running. But the service endpoints are <none>, which suggests that the pod isn\'t being selected by the service. Maybe the pod\'s labels don\'t match the service\'s selector. Let me verify that by describing the pod.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nThe `otel-collector` service has no endpoints, indicating no pods are associated with it. This suggests the service\'s selector does not match any pods, or the pod is misconfigured. I need to check the pod\'s labels and status to confirm if it\'s running and matches the service\'s selector.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl describe pod otel-collector-agent-7fmss -n astronomy-shop"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 553, 'prompt_tokens': 5485, 'total_tokens': 6038, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdfb-cab6-7b22-b6fe-e449021ffda6-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5485, 'output_tokens': 553, 'total_tokens': 6038}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='c5a30b83-e862-47b7-89f6-f7cb3f76ed51'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, 