vice description, the otlp port is 4317/TCP, and the endpoints are <none>. So the service is correctly configured to expose port 4317, but no pods are matching the selector. \n\nWait, the pod's name is otel-collector-agent-7fmss, and the service's selector includes component=agent-collector. The pod's labels include component=agent-collector, so that should match. But why no endpoints? Maybe the service is not properly created, or there's a typo in the selector. \n\nGiven that the service has no endpoints, the most likely cause is that the selector isn't matching any pods. Even though the pod's labels seem to match, there might be a discrepancy. For example, maybe the service's selector is using a different key or value. Or perhaps the pod hasn't been properly registered yet. \n\nBut the pod is running and has been for a few minutes. So the issue is probably a misconfiguration in the service's selector. The product-catalog service is trying to connect to otel-collector:4317, but since the service has no endpoints, it can't resolve the IP, leading to connection refused. \n\nTherefore, the root cause is the misconfigured service selector for otel-collector, leading to no endpoints and connection failures. The faulty component is the otel-collector service in the astronomy-shop namespace.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl apply -f - <<EOF\\napiVersion: v1\\nkind: Service\\nmetadata:\\n  name: otel-collector\\n  namespace: astronomy-shop\\n  labels:\\n    app.kubernetes.io/component: agent-collector\\n    app.kubernetes.io/instance: astronomy-shop\\n    app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: Helm\\n    app.kubernetes.io/name: opentelemetry-collector\\n    app.kubernetes.io/part-of: opentelemetry-collector\\n    app.kubernetes.io/version: 0.142.0\\n    component: agent-collector\\n    helm.sh/chart: opentelemetry-collector-0.142.2\\nspec:\\n  clusterIP: 10.107.202.40\\n  internalTrafficPolicy: Local\\n  ipFamilies:\